WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
This video shows how to connect mdbase collections to the TaskNotes app. We’ll start with a hosted collection, then connect an existing folder on your computer.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Hosted by mdbase: available online, even when your computer is off. No desktop Connector needed for TaskNotes.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Hosted collections can also be mirrored to your computer, so you can work with local Markdown files.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:29.000
On your computer: files stay in an existing folder. Keep mdbase Connect running and the computer reachable. The same TaskNotes app works with either.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:37.600
Start with hosted: open app.tasknotes.dev and choose a collection.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:50.833
Select a collection labelled Hosted by mdbase, then review access.

00:00:50.833 --> 00:01:00.033
Review the permissions, then approve access if you agree.

00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:14.067
Add a task. It is saved in your hosted collection; no local computer is needed.

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:22.067
Already have an mdbase collection on your computer? Connect that folder to TaskNotes without moving its files.

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:35.933
For a local folder, first get the desktop app at mdbase.dev/downloads.

00:01:35.933 --> 00:01:39.933
Install and open mdbase Connect.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:49.467
Name this computer, then choose Continue in browser.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:02:00.400
Sign in if asked, then approve this computer.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:09.400
In Collections, choose Add existing and select your collection folder.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:15.133
Choose the folder containing mdbase.yaml. Its files stay where they are.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:21.933
Back in TaskNotes, open the mdbase collection chooser.

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:35.333
Select the collection listed under your connected computer.

00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:44.566
Review the requested access and setup changes, then approve if you agree.

00:02:44.566 --> 00:02:59.300
Add a task to the local collection.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:06.300
Each task is a Markdown file. Changes you make in TaskNotes are saved back to the collection.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:11.500
The task is now a Markdown file in your existing folder.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.833
Keep mdbase Connect running while other devices use this folder.

00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:24.833
Once both are connected, switch collections in Settings → Change collection.

00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:37.066
Choose a collection you have already approved.

00:03:37.066 --> 00:03:46.066
In the local collection, complete the task.

00:03:46.066 --> 00:03:52.599
The same Markdown file now says status: done.
